## 3. Memory note

**Write** `<memory>/ccs-wg-keepalive-relay.md` (type `project`):

> Pritunl WG clients send `PUT /key/wg/…` to the WG server address on the console port, which listens on loopback only, so every WG tunnel rebuilt about every 45 s. `host_proxy` renders an http relay (`ccs_proxy_wg_keepalive`). Live on ccs-it since 2026-09-28 (PR #165); ccs-ops is not enabled. **Why:** OpenVPN users never saw it. **How to apply:** split "VPN is flaky" reports by protocol; turning the flag off brings the failure back.

**Edit** `MEMORY.md` to add the pointer line.

## 4. Cleanup

**Bash, foreground:**
```bash
herdr agent get wgka          # idle, "focused": false
herdr agent read wgka --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > "$S/inbox/wgka.final"
herdr agent list              # wgka's tab id
herdr tab close <wgka tab_id>
git -C "$R/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive" status --porcelain   # must be empty; never --force
git -C "$R" worktree remove "$R/.claude/worktrees/wg-keepalive" && git -C "$R" worktree prune
git -C "$R" branch -d feat/wg-keepalive-relay
ps -p 48211 -o pid,command    # must be the codex app-server from 21:30
kill 48211
git -C "$R" pull && git -C "$R" worktree list
```

